{title: Softly and Tenderly Jesus Is Calling}
{lyricist: Will L. Thompson}
{composer: Will L. Thompson}
{year: 1880}
{key: G}
{meta: tune THOMPSON}
{meta: variation The hymn, sung to THOMPSON}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags invitation}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Softly and tenderly [C]Jesus is [G]calling,
[G]Calling for [A7]you and for [D]me;
[G]See, on the portals He's [C]waiting and [G]watching,
[G]Watching for [D7]you and for [G]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Refrain}
[D]Come [G]home, [D]come [G]home,
[G]Ye who are [A7]weary, come [D]home;
[G]Earnestly, tenderly, [C]Jesus is [G]calling,
[G]Calling, O [D7]sinner, come [G]home!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Why should we tarry when [C]Jesus is [G]pleading,
[G]Pleading for [A7]you and for [D]me?
[G]Why should we linger and [C]heed not His [G]mercies,
[G]Mercies for [D7]you and for [G]me?
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Time is now fleeting, the [C]moments are [G]passing,
[G]Passing from [A7]you and from [D]me;
[G]Shadows are gathering, [C]deathbeds are [G]coming,
[G]Coming for [D7]you and for [G]me.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]O for the wonderful [C]love He has [G]promised,
[G]Promised for [A7]you and for [D]me!
[G]Though we have sinned, He has [C]mercy and [G]pardon,
[G]Pardon for [D7]you and for [G]me.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
